{
  "slug": "claude-snapshot",
  "name": "Claude Snapshot",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "claude-snapshot exports and imports portable snapshots of your entire Claude Code setup across machines. It captures settings.json, plugins,\nmarketplace registrations, hooks, and global CLAUDE.md files into a single .tar.gz file with a manifest index. Absolute paths are normalized to\n$HOME for cross-machine portability. On apply, it backs up conflicting files as .bak and installs missing plugins automatically. Supports slim\n(config only, ~6KB) and full (with plugin caches for offline restore) export modes.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 commands**.\n\n- **Commands** (4): `apply` (Apply a snapshot to this machine's Claude Code setup), `diff` (Compare a snapshot against your current Claude Code setup), `export` (Export your Claude Code setup as a portable snapshot), `inspect` (Preview snapshot contents without extracting)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-snapshot@claude-community` from `adhenawer/claude-snapshot`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "command",
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Rodolfo Moraes"
  },
